# A book carrying the whole plan convention: a stage entry, a badge,
# all four CriticMarkup kinds, a twin, and a hole. It pins that the
# twin never tangles, that a dodged sigil spelling stays out of the
# index, that only the first mark on a line is indexed, and that the
# hole inside a generated diff becomes a site of its own once the
# diff exists, which is why the first run and the second differ.

exec babble tangle markup.org
cmp markup.org want/pass1.org
cmp m.go want/m.go

exec babble tangle markup.org
cmp markup.org want/pass2.org
cmp m.go want/m.go

-- markup.org --
#+title: the whole plan convention
#+todo: PLANNED(p!) HOLE(h!) FILLING(f!) | LIVE(l!) DROPPED(d@)

* Plan                                                              :plan:

** PLANNED Stage 1: a worked example                              :stage1:
:PROPERTIES:
:CUSTOM_ID: stage-1
:END:

A hole spelled HOLE[(] in prose is not a site, and neither is a
twin suffix written with its hyphens split apart.

#+begin: plan-toc
#+end:

* The program

Prose carrying {++an insertion++} and nothing else.
Prose carrying {--a deletion--} and nothing else.
Prose carrying {~~a replacement~~} and nothing else.
Prose carrying {>>a note<<} and nothing else.
Two marks on one line: {++first++} then {--second--}.

*************** PLANNED stage 1 replaces the block below :stage1:
The badge points a reviewer here.
*************** END

#+name: greet
#+begin_src go :tangle m.go
package m

func Greet() string {
	return "hi"
}
#+end_src

#+name: greet--planned
#+begin_src go :tangle no
package m

func Greet() string {
	panic("HOLE(1): return the configured greeting")
}
#+end_src

#+begin: src-block-diff :old greet :new greet--planned
#+end:
